# Help: NFS over RDMA, client and server, on software RoCE
#
# The RPC-over-RDMA transport (SUNRPC_XPRT_RDMA, net/sunrpc/xprtrdma)
# that the NFS client and server use, over the InfiniBand core with
# its RDMA connection manager and the software RoCE provider, since a
# guest has no HCA.
#
# Prerequisites inlined per the self-containment rule:
# - NFS_FS + NFSD select SUNRPC.
# - INFINIBAND_ADDR_TRANS defaults to y, which an allnoconfig-based
#   merge drops.
#
# Layer builtin/fs/nfs-rdma.config to build it in (=y).
# See: net/sunrpc/Kconfig
# See: https://docs.kernel.org/admin-guide/nfs/nfs-rdma.html

#
# Inlined prerequisites
#
CONFIG_NFS_FS=m
CONFIG_NFSD=m
CONFIG_INFINIBAND=m
CONFIG_INFINIBAND_ADDR_TRANS=y
CONFIG_RDMA_RXE=m

#
# RPC over RDMA
#
CONFIG_SUNRPC_XPRT_RDMA=m
